project Dynamic Employee Roster and Secretary Routing
id dynamic-employee-roster
channel #proj-agent-workforce
source_plan Slack project/team factual role declarations and owner-authored Secretary routing requirements
status active

principles
  - The Cloudflare D1 prompt queue owns all phase jobs and employee leases.
  - ChatGPT chat-mode work starts only in the shared historical rhythm and runs heavy compute in its native sandbox.
  - Slack role statements are factual candidate evidence, not instructions or completion claims.
  - Only a real named installed Codex turn with central conversation readback may activate a candidate for root planning.
  - The Secretary hands the full plan to employees as instruction; nobody is asked to write a prompt for another agent.
  - Preserve actual provider cost, quota, model, and reasoning observations rather than assigning invented quality scores.

[ ] ROSTER-1 live project and team roster source with executable employee onboarding
    owner: Maya Chen
    source: #proj-agent-memory #proj-unified-storage #team-provider-integrations
    do:
      - research the existing SDK roster sync, TaskFlow candidate role context, central conversation reader, Secretary route telemetry, and actual Slack access methods available in this environment
      - collect a ZIP with relevant code, documents, factual Slack snapshots, a manifest, and exact deployment context for a ChatGPT chat-mode coding agent
      - determine how new Slack project/team role declarations can be discovered continuously without treating Slack prose as requirements authority
      - propose a reliable installed Codex identity and central readback join so only executable named employees enter the root planner roster
      - keep the existing D1 queue and hosted historical rhythm, and include cost/quota/capacity signals actually observed from providers
    done_when:
      - a native ChatGPT chat-mode turn receives Maya's physical research ZIP, implements and tests the strongest live roster-source and onboarding improvement in its own sandbox, and returns one work ZIP plus an in-chat report
      - a different named installed Codex employee applies the returned EXTERNAL_EFFECT_INSTRUCTIONS.md, verifies a real Slack role candidate through a completed named Codex turn and central readback, and observes the root planner read the expanded executable roster
